{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994199655500001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bluff-crane-pixel","assignee":"Joe Oakhart","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"25e1d5952b4b9aa850f2ac1da7219c2e7fc6d8f4","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: a88d-bc7e-728b-42b6","material: 1afe92811aeb2e9b","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 12","regver: 83e5f63ad06d893a","verified-at-sha:3b31c454f3820fb8eea683039740c0bd5b99b896","dep absent docs/adr/0013-llm-review-label.md","dep absent infra/compose/gerrit.config","dep absent infra/gerrit/project.config","dep absent infra/gerrit/setup-project.sh"],"signature":"13757ce839352fec6a9e55bec3e77890ed94bf3e98bac1cc554a606e72a78538","signed_at":1782787982310893000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":15},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"DERISK (E4): the submit-requirement predicate is EMPIRICALLY VALID against live Gerrit 3.14.1 — GET /changes/?q=label:LLM-Review=MAX AND -has:unresolved returns HTTP 200 (parses), as do has:unresolved / -has:unresolved / label:Code-Review=MAX. Concrete config to apply (doc-verified syntax):\n[label \"LLM-Review\"]\n  function = NoBlock\n  value = -1 LLM flagged blocking issues\n  value =  0 No score\n  value = +1 LLM approved\n  defaultValue = 0\n  copyCondition = changekind:TRIVIAL_REBASE OR changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE\n[submit-requirement \"LLM-Review\"]\n  submittableIf = label:LLM-Review=MAX AND -has:unresolved\nsubmitWholeTopic is server config: gerrit.config [change] submitWholeTopic = true (set in S2's gerrit.config or here). New labels must use function=NoBlock (blocking functions are rejected; gating is via the submit-requirement).","timestamp":1782686373049312001},{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"## S3 implemented + verified LIVE on Gerrit rebar.solutions.navateam.com — 2026-06-30 (commit ca05de9d9)\n\nThe `rebar` project's refs/meta/config carries the LLM-Review label + submit requirement + ACL; submitWholeTopic is server-global. Applied via setup-project.sh (after granting Administrators refs/meta/config push on All-Projects, server-side, so the normal admin SSH push path works).\n\n**Live config (verified via REST):**\n- Label `LLM-Review`: function=NoBlock, values -1..+1, copyCondition=changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE.\n- Submit requirement `LLM-Review`: submittableIf = `label:LLM-Review=MAX AND -has:unresolved`.\n- Submit requirement `Code-Review`: applicability_expression = `is:false` (DISABLED on rebar) — so LLM-Review is the SOLE applicable gate (bot-only submit, no human Code-Review in v1).\n- ACL: label-LLM-Review granted ONLY to Service Users + Administrators.\n- `change.submitWholeTopic = true` in server gerrit.config [change].\n\n**AC verification (subagent-driven, all PASS):**\n- AC1 — submit blocked until LLM-Review=MAX: a change created via refs/for/master is UNSATISFIED/non-submittable; after admin LLM-Review=+1 -> SATISFIED. (The `-has:unresolved` predicate is present in config; the MAX gate conclusively proven.)\n- AC2 — label exclusive: admin (Administrators) can vote; a regular account (1000001 devuser, Registered Users only) vote was REJECTED with `Applying label \"LLM-Review\": 1 is restricted`.\n- AC3 — copyCondition: a commit-message-only amend (NO_CODE_CHANGE) CARRIED the LLM-Review=+1 to the new patchset; a real rebase onto a moved base (reported TRIVIAL_REBASE, parent 9f3d69e->8891672) DROPPED the vote -> re-review required. Exactly the intended NO_CODE_CHANGE-only behavior.\n- AC4 — submitWholeTopic: changes 22 & 23 on topic `rebar-test`; submitting 22 alone was rejected (\"must be submitted with change 23 ... not ready\"); after approving both, a single submit MERGED both atomically.\n- AC5 — single LLM-Review gate: ADR-0013 records the deliberate single-gate stance (Code-Review override making it non-applicable) + planned evolution (epic 1fa8).\n- Bonus: bot-only submit verified — change 24 with ONLY LLM-Review=MAX shows Code-Review=NOT_APPLICABLE, LLM-Review=SATISFIED (sole applicable gate satisfied).\n\n**Code review (subagent):** VERDICT PASS (no blockers; NITs folded: grep -qxF fixed-string, untracked-groups no-op detection via git add -A + diff --cached, accurate header comment, -1-not-a-veto note in ADR, groups file now includes Registered Users via global:Registered-Users).\n\nThe \"only the bot votes\" end-to-end proof completes in S4 (the bot Service-User account is created there); S3's vote was exercised by an admin (Administrators has the grant) and a regular user was proven unable to vote.","timestamp":1782788993207922001}],"created_at":1782685473948998001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e5199a13-2872-41b2-acc3-e3d31d81577e","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"786b-190d-5e3a-4194"}],"description":"# S3 — Gerrit project + LLM-Review label + submit requirement + submitWholeTopic\n\n## Why\nThis is the gate's integrity rule: a change is submittable ONLY when the deterministic\n`LLM-Review` vote is MAX and there are no unresolved comments. `copyCondition` avoids re-paying\nfor an expensive LLM review on a no-code-change re-upload; `submitWholeTopic` lands whole\nreviewed features atomically. The integrity property is not just \"the label gates submit\" but\n\"ONLY the bot can set the label\" — so a human cannot cast `LLM-Review` and bypass the gate.\nGerrit is pinned to **3.14.1** (d251 docker-compose), so every predicate/feature used here\n(`-has:unresolved`, `copyCondition`, submit requirements) is above its minimum and was\nvalidated to parse against live 3.14.1.\n\n## What\n- Create the `rebar` project in Gerrit (NoteDb).\n- `LLM-Review` label in `refs/meta/config` (project.config): `function=NoBlock`; values `-1..+1`;\n  **`copyCondition = changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE`** (peer-pattern correction). We deliberately do\n  NOT include `changekind:TRIVIAL_REBASE`: a TRIVIAL_REBASE copies the vote even when the change\n  was rebased onto a **different base** (diff is byte-identical but the base moved), which would\n  certify a tree the LLM never reviewed against the new base — the \"copyCondition certifies an\n  unreviewed tree\" risk the Opus red-team flagged. `NO_CODE_CHANGE` pins the parent tree, so it\n  only carries the vote across a true no-op re-upload (e.g. commit-message-only edit). A real\n  rebase therefore drops the vote and forces a fresh review (the safe default for a correctness\n  gate). `function=NoBlock` is **required, not a free choice**: on 3.14.1 a blocking label\n  function is rejected, so blocking comes from the submit requirement.\n- Submit requirement (project.config): `submittableIf = label:LLM-Review=MAX AND -has:unresolved`.\n  This is what blocks submit; the label is advisory on its own. Both predicates validated to\n  parse (HTTP 200) on live Gerrit 3.14.1.\n- `change.submitWholeTopic=true` — set in the **server-level** `gerrit.config` `[change]`\n  section, NOT in project.config (it is a server-global key, silently ignored in project.config).\n  GOTCHA (peer research): topics are **global + un-namespaced**, so a topic name reused in a repo\n  the submitter can't see could silently block submit; for this single-repo PoC that risk is\n  minimal, but adopt a topic naming convention (e.g. `rebar-<feature>`) and document it.\n- Access controls: grant the auto-generated `label-LLM-Review` vote permission to the **Service\n  Users** group; humans may push changes for review but cannot submit without the label and\n  cannot themselves cast `LLM-Review`. The Service Users group is created/wired in **S4**; S3\n  lands config that references it and is testable in S3 by an **admin** casting the vote.\n\n## Scope\nIn: project + `LLM-Review` label (NO_CODE_CHANGE copyCondition) + submit requirement +\nserver-level topic config + the label ACL grant. The \"only the bot votes\" end-to-end proof is\ncompleted in S4 (the bot account does not exist in S3); in S3 the vote is exercised by an admin.\nOut: the bot account + event/vote wiring (S4); replication (S5); GitHub lockdown (S6). Gerrit\nversion is fixed upstream by d251 (3.14.1).\n\n## Files\n- `infra/gerrit/project.config` (pushed to `refs/meta/config`): label, submit requirement,\n  `copyCondition=changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE`, ACL grant.\n- `infra/gerrit/gerrit.config` (server-level): `[change]\\n  submitWholeTopic = true`. (Impl\n  note: same gerrit.config d251 mounts; S3 owns/patches the `[change]` section.)\n- `infra/gerrit/setup-project.sh`: provisions the project + pushes `refs/meta/config`. Impl\n  notes (not separate ACs): (a) **idempotent** — push a fully-declarative project.config via\n  `git push HEAD:refs/meta/config`, guard project creation with check-before-create; (b)\n  **auth** — needs Gerrit admin creds (HTTP password / SSH key), source documented (env/SSM),\n  fail-fast if absent; (c) **dry-run/diff** mode before mutating the live instance.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A change can be pushed for review to the `rebar` project; submit is BLOCKED until\n      `LLM-Review=+1` (MAX) AND no unresolved comments — verified by an admin casting the vote\n      (the bot-only path is proven in S4). Both predicates parse + enforce on 3.14.1.\n- [ ] The `label-LLM-Review` vote permission is granted **exclusively** to the Service Users\n      group: a regular developer cannot cast `LLM-Review` (push `%l=LLM-Review+1` is rejected /\n      not applied) while a Service-Users member can.\n- [ ] `copyCondition=changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE` carries the vote across a no-code-change\n      re-upload (e.g. commit-message-only amend) BUT a genuine rebase onto a moved base\n      (TRIVIAL_REBASE) does NOT carry it — the vote is dropped and re-review is required.\n      Verified on 3.14.1 by (a) a message-only amend keeping the vote and (b) a real rebase\n      dropping it.\n- [ ] `change.submitWholeTopic=true` is set in server-level `gerrit.config` `[change]` (NOT\n      project.config), and demonstrated: two changes under one topic submit atomically and\n      neither submits independently while its topic partner is open.\n- [ ] The submit requirement is the SINGLE code-review vote in v1 (no human Code-Review / CI\n      Verified yet — follow-on epic 1fa8). Record this deliberate single-gate stance + planned\n      evolution in a brief ADR/note.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/gerrit/project.config","reason":"rebar project ACL + LLM-Review label + submit requirement"},{"path":"infra/gerrit/setup-project.sh","reason":"apply project/label/submit-req via refs/meta/config + submitWholeTopic"},{"path":"infra/compose/gerrit.config","reason":"change.submitWholeTopic=true (server-global)"},{"path":"docs/adr/0013-llm-review-label.md","reason":"ADR for single LLM-Review label + submit requirement"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["depends_on","786b-190d-5e3a-4194"],["parent","d251-05e1-eb55-43b2"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"d251-05e1-eb55-43b2","parent_status_uuid":"1948e29c-4ed3-488d-8540-72cf700b7ac5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["gerrit","config"],"ticket_id":"a88d-bc7e-728b-42b6","ticket_type":"story","title":"infra: S3 — Gerrit project + LLM-Review label + submit requirement + submitWholeTopic","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e91bd6e9-3bbf-4cfe-8b95-7ae2c40e8e0b","e5199a13-2872-41b2-acc3-e3d31d81577e","c1b87626-4374-4b99-842f-a74451a6f684","013a5ab5-72b5-46d5-a26e-021d29acb893","c8b0e5e6-1940-4147-9b62-34baa91d43d6","d358556d-7f77-47db-ab9c-decabfaddaea","e5b58f3d-34d0-4030-b9e6-2371b1a63276","87db3410-07d7-4376-85e7-780c3f4ce620","b4133f5d-0de6-414c-aedf-6917d896016c","4d455e46-48fd-41d5-b9fb-5f33fa4c1d7c","18ff13ce-7452-4c1c-9b14-f63471506f33","a7cbe137-41cc-4a17-b614-985e0968a008","36a0227c-b256-4200-ab0e-419b94c16e81","bba6b6e6-5fe6-4610-a057-dc8ce05eb418","6636eb4f-fca0-47e8-99ff-f7708f09dd85","9236b991-7bf8-4c00-b737-15a1b511dba3","e0b57cca-0177-489a-8689-4c97ca55d60c","1948e29c-4ed3-488d-8540-72cf700b7ac5","7baff45a-9c2f-4feb-88f4-821520812e50","13251537-e10d-437f-a3f6-db76b7a82cac","03949ece-ef6e-4c07-9cb2-de66e13ec049"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994199655500001,"uuid":"da7d0ddc-1fa2-44b6-bac3-fa285ca3c396"}